Pedagogy’s hinge in *Places of Learning: Media, Architecture, Pedagogy*, MIT Press 2005 is the architectural/performative threshold that makes inside and outside, private and public, spectator and participant continuous and discontinuous at the same time in order to re-work personal and social boundaries.

The hinge is built up in the book around a consistent set of museum, settlement-house and verbatim performance sites:

* The U.S. Holocaust Memorial Museum, Washington D.C., the entry ramp, Hall of Witness and underground axis as an architectural pedagogy of witness that hinges public history and interiorized memory;
* The Jane Addams Hull-House Museum, Chicago, with its porches, doorways and domestic/public rooms re-activated as a settlement-house hinge. The Hull-House discussion is developed through its own programming, including the installation/intervention *Bravehearts: Men in Skirts*, which Ellsworth uses as an embodied, street-level hinge on gendered inside/outside boundaries;
* The Manhattan Children’s Museum’s Art Inside Out, the programme that literally moves children’s work from the gallery interior to the street façade and back, a classic inside/outside curatorial hinge;
* Anna Deavere Smith’s documentary theatre, *Fires in the Mirror* / *Twilight: Los Angeles, 1992*, treated as a performative hinge that puts theatrical inside and civic outside, performer/audience, testimony and public space into relation.

Those four hinge clusters — Holocaust Museum, Hull-House Museum with *Bravehearts: Men in Skirts* as its performative illustration, CMOM Art Inside Out, and Anna Deavere Smith — are the cases Ellsworth returns to at length.

The Chicago Symphony Orchestra’s Education Center / Symphony Center education initiatives are not developed as a pedagogy’s hinge case in *Places of Learning*. The book’s architectural and performance cases are museum, settlement and testimonial performance sites that explicitly stage the wall/street, interior/exterior, private/public relation; the CSO education facility does not appear in that hinge argument.

Hence the item not used as a hinge illustration is E.

4.text:
E. Chicago Symphony Orchestra's Education Center

On the evidence from the previous round the hinge cases Ellsworth actually develops in *Places of Learning: Media, Architecture, Pedagogy* are the museum, settlement and performance thresholds that physically and socially work inside/outside, private/public, spectator/participant.

That core set is:

* U.S. Holocaust Memorial Museum – the ramped entry / Hall of Witness as an architectural pedagogy of witnessing;
* Jane Addams Hull-House Museum – porch, doorways and domestic/public rooms as a historic settlement hinge, with the museum’s own programming used to illustrate the hinge, e.g. *Bravehearts: Men in Skirts*;
* Manhattan Children’s Museum’s Art Inside Out – the literal movement of children’s work from gallery interior to street and back;
* Anna Deavere Smith’s verbatim documentary theatre, *Fires in the Mirror* / *Twilight: Los Angeles, 1992* – a performative hinge collapsing performer/audience, self/other, story and event.

*Bravehearts: Men in Skirts* is consistently treated by the majority of the group as taken up by Ellsworth as an embodied, street/body performative hinge that reconfigures gendered and national inside/outside boundaries, and in Colleague 4’s account is explicitly linked to the Hull-House discussion.

The Chicago Symphony Orchestra’s Education Center / Symphony Center initiatives do not appear as one of those hinge case studies in *Places of Learning*. The book’s architectural and performative cases are museum, settlement and testimonial/performance sites that stage a threshold between interior learning space and exterior public space; a conventional music-education facility is not mobilised for the pedagogy’s hinge argument. That is the outlier among the six options.

The minority claim that *Bravehearts* is absent and that the CSO is discussed, advanced by Colleague 8, is outweighed by the convergence of Colleagues 2,3,4,5,6,7,9 and 10 on the four core hinge exemplars plus Bravehearts, with E as the non-example.

